
"""
Combined program: Nutrition Calculator + USDA Food Classifier
=============================================================
Two independent programs merged into one file. Running it executes the
nutrition calculator first (prompts + DRI report), then the USDA food
classifier (prompts + filtered nutrient table) - each produces exactly
the same output it did standalone.

--- PROGRAM 1: Nutrition Calculator ---
Calculates daily maintenance calories and full Dietary Reference Intakes
(RDA / Adequate Intake) plus Tolerable Upper Intake Levels (UL) for all
fat-soluble vitamins, water-soluble vitamins, macrominerals, and trace
minerals, across all life stages (infants through older adults, pregnancy,
and lactation).

Energy method (evidence-based):
  - Adults (>=19): IOM/National Academies (2023) Estimated Energy Requirement
    (EER) equations, Table S-3. Four activity categories (inactive, low_active,
    active, very_active) defined by Physical Activity Level (PAL) ranges; the
    activity effect is built into each sex-specific equation. Height in cm.
  - Children/adolescents (3-18) and infants (0-3): IOM EER equations.
  - Pregnancy/lactation: IOM energy increments added to maintenance.

Macronutrient method (evidence-based):
  - Protein: IOM RDA in g/kg/day by life stage (0.8 g/kg for adults), the
    established Recommended Dietary Allowance. Reported %kcal is checked
    against the protein AMDR (10-35%).
  - Fat and carbohydrate: IOM Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Ranges
    (AMDR), expressed as a percent of total energy. Targets are taken at the
    midpoint of the age-appropriate AMDR:
        Fat   - infants <1y: ~40-55% (AI, no AMDR); 1-3y: 30-40%; 4-18y: 25-35%;
                >=19y: 20-35%.
        Carb  - >=1y: 45-65%.
  - Water: IOM total-water Adequate Intake (AI) by life stage
    (3.7 L/day men, 2.7 L/day women for adults; includes water from food).

Calorie-deficit method (weight loss, adults only):
  - Energy : maintenance - 500 kcal/day (a moderate deficit, ~0.45 kg/week).
  - Protein: minimum 1.6 g/kg body weight - well above the 0.8 g/kg RDA, to
    spare lean mass during the deficit (consistent with higher-protein
    weight-loss evidence; stays within the protein AMDR).
  - Fat    : minimum 20% of deficit calories (hormone and fat-soluble-vitamin
    floor).
  - Carb   : minimum 130 g/day (the carbohydrate RDA, set to meet the brain's
    glucose requirement). Remaining energy after the protein and fat floors is
    assigned to carbohydrate, never dropping below 130 g.
  Not shown for infants, children, pregnant, or lactating people, for whom an
  energy deficit is not appropriate.

This is a single self-contained file. Nutrient values are the U.S. Dietary
Reference Intakes from the NIH/National
Academies DRI Summary Tables (NBK545442) and the underlying IOM reports,
reported in their official units (e.g. ug RAE, mg NE, ug DFE).
Sources for all formulas/values are documented in research_summary.md.
"""

